WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:03.830
The Transformers franchise has been nothing
if not divisive.

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:09.230
While some fans have remained resolutely loyal,
the majority of critics, and plenty of average

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:15.210
moviegoers, have criticized its emphasis on
noisy CGI style over storytelling substance.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:20.390
Still, the series has raked in a combined
total of over $4 billion, proving there's

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.260
an audience for this series.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.260
Or there was, anyway.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:29.860
In 2018, Paramount tabled plans to make a
Transformers 7 for the foreseeable future.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:34.739
Why would the studio stop the machine that
transformed a toy line into a multi-billion-dollar

00:00:34.739 --> 00:00:36.739
global cinematic affair?

00:00:36.739 --> 00:00:39.719
The answers might surprise you.

00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:42.999
Critical disdain and financial struggles

00:00:42.999 --> 00:00:48.239
No studio wants to invest years of development
and millions of dollars into films that critics

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:50.449
end up trashing with negative reviews.

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:55.799
While that concern is usually secondary to
box office grosses, the reality is that with

00:00:55.799 --> 00:01:00.170
Transformers, Paramount was seeing both dwindle
at roughly proportionate rates.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:04.960
Maybe the series' downward-trending Rotten
Tomatoes scores indicated a larger problem.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.650
Perhaps the average moviegoer finally saw
what the critics saw in these films, and consequently

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:11.780
chose not to see them anymore.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:16.409
It's hardly unusual for action blockbusters
to earn middling-to-negative reviews, but

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:20.950
the Transformers pattern was clear: the movies
were entertaining fewer and fewer people as

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:21.950
they went along.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:25.240
"I don't know what you're hiding but I don't
want anything to do with it, so goodbye, you

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.620
never saw me, I got bagels to shmear.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:27.540
Vanish!"

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:34.580
Following the second entry's series high of
$402.1 million in receipts, 2009's Revenge

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:39.859
of the Fallen, domestic ticket sales have
dropped with each installment in the franchise.

00:01:39.859 --> 00:01:44.409
These movies are extremely expensive, and
if audiences are snubbing sequels to such

00:01:44.409 --> 00:01:49.999
a degree that more than $100 million disappeared
between chapters, maybe it's time for Paramount

00:01:49.999 --> 00:01:51.289
to reassess.

00:01:51.289 --> 00:01:58.110
It's a worldwide trend, too, as 2017's The
Last Knight raked in $500 million less internationally

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:01.819
than its predecessor, 2014's Age of Extinction.

00:02:01.819 --> 00:02:03.979
Bye to the Bay

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:07.799
Very few people are qualified to direct a
$200 million movie.

00:02:07.799 --> 00:02:13.000
It requires an immense amount of technical
skill, leadership, coordination, and planning.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.980
That is why, love him or hate him, studios
respect Michael Bay and his particular set

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:18.980
of skills.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:23.110
Bay's been making noise about leaving the
franchise for years, but Paramount has kept

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:24.900
making him offers he couldn't refuse.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.890
"A gigantic pile of money."

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:31.720
But as of 2017, he has officially departed
the franchise.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:36.510
Without Bay, the studio simply doesn't have
a go-to guy that can guarantee the successful

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.580
production of a blockbuster on this scale.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.700
A convoluted narrative

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:46.590
It's generous to say that the Transformers
franchise has really never made a lick of

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:47.590
sense.

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:52.190
But at least the first movie's plot was simple
and elegant: a boy finds out his car is actually

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:56.230
an alien robot, and the two go on an adventure
to recover a magic cube.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.990
It was just outlandish and silly enough to
work.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:04.140
From there, however, Bay and his stable of
writers have churned out an increasingly convoluted

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:05.140
narrative.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:09.700
In Revenge of the Fallen, Optimus Prime was
brought back to life by an ancient dagger

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:12.050
disguised as a pile of sand.

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:17.340
Then in Dark of the Moon, we learned that
the Decepticons had actually been within range

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:21.970
of Earth for decades, and were simply hiding
and waiting for the right moment to reveal

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:22.970
themselves.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:28.160
Age of Extinction went even further back in
time, claiming there were prehistoric dinosaur

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:29.160
Transformers.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:32.739
Then The Last Knight revealed that Bumblebee
was a World War II veteran.

00:03:32.739 --> 00:03:37.780
And that Shia LaBeouf's character was a descendant
of the Knights of the Round Table.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:38.780
Uh-huh.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.280
"It is I, Merlin.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.980
The wizard?

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.340
Ha, remember me?"

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.280
Where could the writers have possibly gone
from there?

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.150
Fortunately, it doesn't look like we'll have
to find out.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.790
Paramount's brand priorities

00:03:55.790 --> 00:04:01.450
Movie franchises often strive to expand the
overall brand with success across other mediums,

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:05.070
but that's easier said than done, and Transformers
is proof.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:09.090
The property has maintained strength in the
action figure market, but there's been little

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.900
growth in other areas.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:15.730
The publishing license remains stuck at a
B-tier comic book company, while the latest

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:20.220
tie-in video games have been met with middling
reviews, or worse.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:24.410
Meanwhile, Paramount has plenty of other big
movies for well-known and beloved intellectual

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:29.230
properties lined up for 2019, which means
a lot of money is already at stake.

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:33.940
Currently on the slate are the long-awaited
Top Gun sequel, another Terminator reboot,

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.600
and a Sonic the Hedgehog adaptation.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:41.190
They're all high-profile releases based on
huge brands, and they're each risky in its

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:42.190
own way.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:46.160
Given all the money on the line with these
films, it's only logical that Paramount wouldn't

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:50.930
want to further strain its resources on a
seventh Transformers.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:52.660
The Bumblebee gambit

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:57.060
Paramount might also be unwilling to proceed
with Transformers 7 until the results are

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.790
in for the Bumblebee prequel, technically
Transformers 6.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:05.370
If it turns out to be the franchise's last
hope, it's in good hands; the director is

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:10.130
the supremely talented Travis Knight, who
delivered the magnificent Kubo and the Two

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.130
Strings.

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:15.000
If it bombs, that's one more reason why the
studio would be right to wait and get its

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.460
Transformers house in order before sinking
any more money into it.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:23.760
Should it flop, that'll probably be the end
of the line for the franchise as we know it.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.100
Reboot time

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:30.990
Franchise reboots have become fairly common
lately, and a complete Transformers do-over

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:33.020
would achieve a lot of things at once.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:37.440
It would wipe out the absolutely bonkers backstory
that's built up to this point.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:41.830
It could earn a fresh start with fans, provided
Paramount shows proof that they've learned

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:42.880
from past mistakes.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:47.040
And there's even a chance critics might learn
to like the series, so long as there's enough

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.430
heart, brains, and good old-fashioned fun.

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:54.490
All it takes is one press of the reset button,
and Transformers can re-emerge as the franchise

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:59.120
it was always supposed to be: one every blockbuster
fan on the planet can get into.

